# One change at a time

A small experiment starts with a question you can test. Choose an input to change, an output to measure, and conditions to keep the same.

## A simple example

Make two paper beams with different folds. Compare them using the same paper, span, and load. Record the differences before drawing a conclusion.

**Useful relationship:** total time = trials × time per trial

## Pause and try

Propose one experiment. State your question and choose the one variable you will change.

